  "body": "One of the most interesting things about UA strings is how they differ, both between platforms of the same browser and between versions of the same browser within a platform.\r\n\r\nAlthough you can kind of figure this out from the prose, e.g. it says that on desktop `<geckoVersion>` is frozen as `\"20100101\"`, I think the examples could make this clear at a glance with some extra markup.\r\n\r\nHere is a quick mockup of what this would look like using `<mark>`. It only marks up differences within the same platform; maybe a different-color `<mark>` could be used for highlight the mobile-vs.-desktop differences, or maybe that's not necessary since they're already side-by-side:\r\n\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/617481/152025343-bdf86b93-9252-4043-a69a-c5c28f03b7da.png)",
